---
// Az adatkezelési tájékoztató angol változata — a magyar párja:
// src/pages/adatvedelmi-nyilatkozat.astro. A két lap tartalma együtt
// változik, a hatálydátummal együtt.
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

// A tájékoztató verziódátuma. Érdemi módosításkor át kell írni.
const hatalyos = 'October 15, 2026';
---

<Base
  cim="Privacy notice"
  leiras="What data triox.hu processes, what happens to it, who receives it, and how you can have it deleted."
>
  <section class="band">
    <div class="wrap prose jogi">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
      <h1>Privacy notice</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        This notice covers the processing of personal data related to your use of the triox.hu
        website: what we ask you for, what happens to it, who receives it, and what you can do if you
        change your mind.
      </p>
      <p class="jogi__datum">Effective: {hatalyos}</p>

      <h2>Who processes your data</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Triox Informatika Kft.</strong><br />
        Registered office: 1106 Budapest, Kada utca 133., Hungary<br />
        Company registration no.: 01-09-449388<br />
        Tax ID: 13316460-2-42<br />
        Email: <a href="mailto:info@triox.hu">info@triox.hu</a>
      </p>
      <p>
        We have not appointed a data protection officer—the law does not require one for our
        activities. Please send any data protection questions to{' '}
        <a href="mailto:info@triox.hu">info@triox.hu</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        This notice applies to the triox.hu website, both the Hungarian and the English pages. The
        client portal (support.triox.hu) and remote assistance (rd.triox.hu) linked from the website
        are separate services that our existing clients use under their contracts.
      </p>
      <p>
        This is an English translation of our Hungarian privacy notice. If the two versions differ,
        the <a href="/adatvedelmi-nyilatkozat/" hreflang="hu" lang="hu">Hungarian version</a> prevails.
      </p>

      <h2>The contact form</h2>
      <p>
        There is only one place on the website where we ask for your data: the{' '}
        <a href="/en/contact/">contact form</a>. Your <strong>name</strong>, <strong>email
        address</strong> and <strong>message</strong> are required—without them we cannot reply.
        Your <strong>company name</strong> and <strong>phone number</strong> are optional.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>What happens after you submit it?</strong> Two emails are sent. One goes to us, with
        the content of your inquiry; the other goes to you as a confirmation. The confirmation
        deliberately does not include the text of your message, only your name—so the form cannot be
        used to make us send text to other people’s addresses.
      </p>
      <p>
        We <strong>do not store your data in a database</strong>. Your inquiry stays in our email,
        just as if you had written to us directly.
      </p>

      <h3>Purpose and legal basis</h3>
      <p>
        We use your data only to answer your inquiry and—if that is what you are asking for—to
        prepare a quote. We do not use it for marketing and we do not send newsletters.
      </p>
      <p>
        Legal basis: taking steps at your request prior to entering into a contract
        [GDPR Article 6(1)(b)]. If your inquiry is not aimed at a contract, the legal basis is our
        legitimate interest in replying to you [GDPR Article 6(1)(f)].
      </p>

      <h3>How long we keep it</h3>
      <p>
        We keep your inquiry and the related correspondence <strong>until you ask us to delete
        it</strong>. A single email to <a href="mailto:info@triox.hu">info@triox.hu</a> is enough,
        and we will delete it within 30 days.
      </p>
      <p>
        There is one exception: if your inquiry led to a contract, Hungarian accounting law
        (Act C of 2000 on Accounting) requires us to keep data related to invoicing for 8 years. We
        must keep that data until the end of this period, even if you ask us to delete it.
      </p>

      <h3>Preventing abuse</h3>
      <p>
        To keep the form from being used to send bulk email, we accept only a limited number of
        submissions from one network (IP address) within a short period. To do this, we store the
        sender’s <strong>IP address for no more than 20 minutes</strong> together with a counter,
        after which it is deleted automatically. Legal basis: our legitimate interest in keeping
        the service secure [GDPR Article 6(1)(f)].
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies, data stored in your browser and visitor statistics</h2>
      <p>
        The website <strong>does not use cookies</strong>.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Language setting.</strong> If you click the Hungarian or the US flag in the header,
        we save your choice in your browser’s local storage (localStorage, key{' '}
        <code>triox-nyelv</code>) so that you get the site in the same language next time. It stays
        on your device, never reaches us, and you can remove it at any time by clearing your
        browser data. If you have not made a choice, we go by your browser’s language
        setting—and we do not store that either.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Visitor statistics.</strong> We measure traffic with Cloudflare Web Analytics,{' '}
        <strong>without cookies</strong>: how many page views there were, on which pages, where
        visitors came from, from which country and on which device, and how fast the page loaded.
        The measurement does not identify visitors and does not track them on other websites.
        Legal basis: our legitimate interest in improving the website [GDPR Article 6(1)(f)].
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Delivering the site.</strong> As with any website, the server processes your
        browser’s technical data (IP address, browser type, the page requested) to display the page
        and to fend off attacks. This is done by our hosting provider, Cloudflare.
      </p>

      <h2>Who receives your data</h2>
      <p>
        We do not sell data, and we do not pass it on for marketing. To run the website, however,
        we use external providers who act as data processors:
      </p>
      <table class="jogi__tabla">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Provider</th>
            <th scope="col">What it does</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Cloudflare, Inc.</td>
            <td>Hosting the website, running the form endpoint and its rate limit, and the cookieless visitor statistics</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Microsoft Ireland Operations Limited</td>
            <td>Sending and storing the emails from the form (Microsoft 365 / Exchange Online)</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p>
        These providers may also process data outside the European Union, typically in the United
        States. The legal framework for such transfers is provided by the European Commission’s
        adequacy decision and by its standard contractual clauses.
      </p>
      <p>
        Beyond this, we disclose data only when the law requires us to—for example, at the request
        of a public authority or a court.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>You may ask us at any time to</p>
      <ul>
        <li>tell you what data of yours we process (access);</li>
        <li>correct inaccurate data (rectification);</li>
        <li>delete your data (erasure);</li>
        <li>restrict processing while a disputed matter is being resolved;</li>
        <li>provide your data in a machine-readable format (data portability);</li>
        <li>and you may object to processing that is based on legitimate interest.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Write to <a href="mailto:info@triox.hu">info@triox.hu</a>, and{' '}
        <strong>we will reply within 30 days</strong>. Fulfilling your request is free of charge.
      </p>

      <h2>How we protect your data</h2>
      <p>
        The website is available only over an encrypted connection (HTTPS), and the form data
        reaches us the same way. We store inquiries in our Microsoft 365 mailbox, which only our
        staff can access. The credentials used for sending email exist only on the server side and
        are never exposed to the browser.
      </p>

      <h2>If you have a complaint</h2>
      <p>
        Please contact us first at <a href="mailto:info@triox.hu">info@triox.hu</a>—most questions
        are resolved fastest this way. Regardless, you may turn to the supervisory authority at any
        time:
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Hungarian National Authority for Data Protection and Freedom of Information (NAIH)</strong><br />
        Address: 1055 Budapest, Falk Miksa utca 9–11., Hungary<br />
        Mailing address: 1363 Budapest, Pf. 9.<br />
        Phone: +36 1 391 1400<br />
        Email: <a href="mailto:ugyfelszolgalat@naih.hu">ugyfelszolgalat@naih.hu</a><br />
        Website: <a href="https://naih.hu" rel="noopener">naih.hu</a>
      </p>
      <p>
        If your rights are violated, you may also go to court. Under Hungarian law, you may bring
        the case before the regional court of your place of residence or stay.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this notice</h2>
      <p>
        If the way the website works changes, we will update this notice as well. The top of the
        page always shows the date from which the current text is effective.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .jogi {
    max-width: 46rem;
  }
  .jogi__datum {
    font-family: var(--f-util);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    color: var(--c-steel);
    padding-bottom: 1.4rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--c-line);
  }
  .jogi h3 {
    margin-top: 1.8rem;
  }
  .jogi__tabla {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    margin: 1.4rem 0 1.6rem;
    font-size: 0.94rem;
  }
  .jogi__tabla th,
  .jogi__tabla td {
    text-align: left;
    padding: 0.6rem 0.9rem 0.6rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--c-line);
    vertical-align: top;
  }
  .jogi__tabla th {
    font-family: var(--f-util);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--c-steel);
    font-weight: 400;
  }
</style>
